# Plan Reactor-Aware Mission Request Scheduling - Software Design Description

> Define how normalized ingress becomes reactor-visible demand and how a trusted consumer schedules native mission-request application without letting connectors or janitor posture pull board lanes directly.

**SRS:** [SRS.md](SRS.md)

## Overview

This voyage corrects the too-direct janitor bridge by inserting a Keel-native
communication and staging layer between normalized external ingress and
planning mutation. Provider runtimes such as Keeper still normalize GitHub
traffic and own transport acknowledgements, but they first submit a typed
ingress record into Keel. That record becomes authored demand visible to
Keel-native reactors and read models. A separately trusted consumer decides
whether and when to schedule mission-request `draft` and `apply`; other
reactors remain observers, enrichers, or escalators rather than lane-pullers.

## Context & Boundaries

The relevant boundaries are already present in the repo:

- `ping` and `poke` are conversational surfaces and should stay that way.
- Formal mission requests are structured planning ingress with only `apply`
  allowed to mutate board state.
- Cross-aggregate automation inside Keel belongs in the application process
  manager and its reactors, not in provider adapters.

This voyage therefore does not make GitHub connectors, janitor posture, or
free-form comms direct board-mutators. It introduces a typed ingress record
that uses Keel communication and reactor machinery to surface pending work
inside the engine before a trusted consumer schedules any mutation.

```text
GitHub issue / comment / workflow signal
                  |
                  v
        Spoke connector and janitor producer
      normalize + attach replay and trust data
                  |
                  v
        Keel typed ingress record / notice
   envelope + replay_identity + trust_context
        + scheduling_state=pending
                  |
                  v
      Keel read models and process-manager reactors
         become aware, score, summarize, escalate
                  |
                  v
            Trusted consumer only
     schedule -> mission request draft/apply
                  |
                  v
        board mutation + acknowledgement payload
                  |
                  v
          Spoke transport delivery and retries
```

